The native transport links the OpenAI Codex SDK at commit
4ebc485ca321243727539187169425fcf972f2c4, released as
rust-v0.163.0-alpha.10.2, under its Apache-2.0 license.

The build adds raw outgoing JSON envelopes and an optional server name to the
SDK transport in a private build checkout, and refuses to create a new machine
enrollment. Gateway files added to that checkout (native-relay/sdk-overlay) and
small string patches (scripts/native-relay-sdk-patches.mjs) also send an unknown
pong when the relay ends a remote stream, keep a re-initialized stream open,
count silent inbound drops and sequence gaps, and add disconnect error kinds to
two existing warnings. SDK license and notice files must accompany distributed
relay binaries. The gateway's relay implementation is MIT.

The relay also uses tracing and tracing-subscriber (MIT), already part of the
pinned SDK dependency graph, to record audited SDK transport events.
